<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bistŏnes</span></b> , um,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βίστονες</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the Bistones</i>, <i>a Thracian people south of Mount Rhodope</i>, <i>not far from Abdera</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 11,
				18, § 42</span></i>.—In the poets, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In gen., for <i>the
				Thracians</i>, <i><span class="en">Luc. 7, 569</span></i>; acc.
			Bistonas, <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 3, 83</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 2,
			76</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bistŏnĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βιστόνιος</span>,
				<i>pertaining to the Bistones.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>Bistonian</i>: plăgae. <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
			30</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> In
			gen., <i>Thracian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rupes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
				2</span></i>
			 (3), 30, 36: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viri,</span>”
				<i>the Thracians</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 13, 430</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aqua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. H.
					2, 90</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sarissae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					P. 1, 3, 59</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Minerva (as goddess of the warlike Thracians),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ib.
					377</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tereus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg. Cul. 251</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tyrannus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the Thracian king Diomedes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					2, 163</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aves, i. e. grues,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					200</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turbo,</span>”
				i. e. <i>a violent north wind</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					767</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ensis Tydei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 586</span></i>
			: chelys, <i>the lyre of the Thracian
			Orpheus</i>, Claud. Rapt. Pros. praef. 2, 8 al.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bistŏ-nĭa</span></b> , ae,
				f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βιστονια</span>, <i>Thrace</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bistoniae magnus alumnus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Orpheus</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 3, 159</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bistŏnis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>, =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βιστονίς</span>, <i>pertaining to the Bistones</i>, for <i>Thracian</i>: ora. <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 15</span></i> (16), 344: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					P. 2, 9, 54</span></i>
			: ales i. e. <i>Procne</i>, <i>wife
				of the Thracian king Tereus</i>, <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Agam. 670</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Subst., <i>a Thracian woman</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bistonidum crines,</span>”
				<i>of the Thracian Bacchantes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 19, 20</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Verg. Cir. 164</span></i>, ubi v.
			Sillig.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
